Manufacturing Yield Remains a Critical Challenge

Fan-out production involves complex manufacturing steps, including die placement, molding, redistribution-layer fabrication and final testing. Die shift, warpage, conductive defects and material interactions can reduce yield and increase cost per qualified package.

Suppliers therefore compete through process control, inspection, materials engineering, equipment capability and integration expertise.

